# IDF 6.0 Source Rules

## Includes

- Driver headers no longer pull FreeRTOS — add `#include "freertos/FreeRTOS.h"` etc. explicitly when needed.
- One component manifest per app component: `main/idf_component.yml`.

## Peripheral init pattern

```c
static const char *TAG = "module";

esp_err_t init_peripheral(void) {
    peripheral_handle_t handle = NULL;
    peripheral_config_t cfg = { /* ... */ };

    esp_err_t err = peripheral_driver_install(&cfg, &handle);
    if (err != ESP_OK) {
        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "install failed: %s", esp_err_to_name(err));
        return err;
    }

    err = peripheral_driver_enable(handle);
    if (err != ESP_OK) {
        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "enable failed: %s", esp_err_to_name(err));
        peripheral_driver_uninstall(handle);
        return err;
    }
    return ESP_OK;
}
```

Use `ESP_RETURN_ON_ERROR`, `ESP_GOTO_ON_ERROR`, or `errdefer`-style `goto fail` — never fall through on failure.

## Strict compilation

- Explicit casts; no unused variables (`(void)x` or remove).
- Prototype all static functions; include every used header.
- No orphan sections — fix linker fragments, don't suppress with `CONFIG_COMPILER_ORPHAN_SECTIONS=place` unless intentional.
- C default **gnu23**, C++ **gnu++26** — fix new standard warnings.

## GPIO / pull / OD

- `io_od_mode` removed from RMT/MCPWM configs — call `gpio_od_enable()` separately.
- Pull-up/down removed from some driver structs — use `gpio_set_pull_mode()`.
